  "visual_findings": [
    "Broad illuminated rock caps now sit above the shaded front face on the long north edges, instead of presenting the authored face upside down.",
    "The approached, contacted and damaged rim keeps its scale and existing texture material. No new clipping or world displacement is visible in the reviewed pairs.",
    "The newly exposed north rim after mining also gains the correct upright face.",
    "Both adjoining biomes remain unchanged; changed Moss sections preserve material identity.",
    "Existing sideways west rocks, full-elbow corners, rectangular step underlaps and the boxed mined opening remain conspicuous and unresolved.",
    "The fixture-triggered reward icon is identical in each pair; it does not establish normal UI behavior."
  ],
